          "description": [
            "Source code.",
            "DISCASM.",
            "Generic indexer for TAB-delimited genome position files.",
            "The main purpose of HTSlib is to provide access to genomic information files, both alignment data (SAM, BAM, and CRAM formats) and variant data (VCF and BCF formats). The library also provides interfaces to access and index genome reference data in FASTA format and tab-delimited files with genomic coordinates. It is utilized and incorporated into both SAMtools and BCFtools.",
            "C library for high-throughput sequencing data formats.",
            "DISCASM aims to extract reads that map to reference genomes in a discordant fashion and optionally include reads that do not map to the genome at all, and perform a de novo transcriptome assembly of these reads. DISCASM relies on the output from STAR (as run via STAR-Fusion), and supports de novo transcriptome assembly using Trinity or Oases. - https://github.com/DISCASM/DISCASM/wiki.",
            "C library and command line tools for high-throughput sequencing data formats.",
            "A set of useful functions for processing admixture proportion files from the population structure analysis softwares STRUCTURE, TESS, ADMIXTURE, BAPS, fastSTRUCTURE etc. The package contains functions to read runs, tabulate runs, summarise runs, plot runs, estimate K using Evanno method, export clumpp files, export distruct files and generate barplots.",
            "An R package to analyse and visualise admixture proportions from STRUCTURE, fastSTRUCTURE, TESS, ADMIXTURE etc."
          ],
          "documentation": [
